---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Email from '../components/Email.astro';
---
<Base title="Speaking" description="Talks, panels and guest lectures on AI security, cloud security, incident response and security leadership.">
  <div class="page-intro">
    <h1>Speaking</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      I speak with engineering, security and leadership audiences about how AI is changing security and what
      teams can do about it.
    </p>
    <p>
      I bring more than eight years in cybersecurity, hands-on experience securing cloud products, and an MBA
      lens on how security decisions get made and funded. I can give a talk, join a panel, guest lecture for a
      class, or be a podcast guest, and I can tailor any topic below for technical or non-technical audiences.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="section-head"><h2>Topics</h2></div>
  <ul class="topics">
    <li>
      <h3>Threat modeling AI agents</h3>
      <p>What changes when software has tools, memory and permissions, and the controls that actually matter.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Securing AI systems</h3>
      <p>Prompt injection, AI supply chain risk, and how to review an AI feature before it ships.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>AI in security operations</h3>
      <p>Where AI helps defenders today, where it adds risk, and how to tell the difference.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Cloud and product security</h3>
      <p>Building security into products that customers rely on, from design reviews to release.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Third-party and AI vendor risk</h3>
      <p>What changes when vendors connect through tokens and APIs instead of network logins.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Lessons from recent breaches</h3>
      <p>What major incidents teach about incident response, disclosure and accountability.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Security for executives and boards</h3>
      <p>Turning technical risk into decisions leaders can make and fund.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Careers in cybersecurity</h3>
      <p>Getting into the field, growing in it, and getting your first conference talk accepted.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <div class="section-head"><h2>Invite me</h2></div>
  <p class="prose">
    For conferences, podcasts, panels or guest lectures, email <Email />.
    Bios and a headshot are on the <a href="/about/#bios">About page</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
